BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Trinity Episcopal Church
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241205T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241205T193000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;WKST=SU;UNTIL=20241219T045959Z;BYDAY=TH
EXDATE;TZID=America/New_York:20241212T180000
DTSTAMP:20260731T040100Z
UID:4ajtcfa33q60hba9uhb2ku31ol@google.com
CREATED:20241202T220158Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Explore your faith\, deepen yourdevotional practices\, and m
 ake community with other writers in ourparish. </p><p><span>Greg Tolliver i
 s leading</span><span> </span><span>this small writinggroup in the Trinity 
 Library on </span><b>Thursday evenings6:00–7:30pm</b><span> during Advent (
 </span><u>Dec. 5\, 12\,19</u><span>) and once during Christmastide (</span>
 <u>Jan. 2</u><span>). </span></p><p>Guided by the themes ofAdvent—faith\, h
 ope\, peace\, joy\, and love—this group will use sacred art andwriting prom
 pts to spiritually prepare for and celebrate the Christmasseason. <span>All
  genres and levels ofexperience are welcome!  Please join us!</span></p>For
  moreinformation\, contact Stephanie Smallwood (<a href="mailto:ChurchYear@
 TrinityBloomington.org">ChurchYear@TrinityBloomington.org</a>).
LAST-MODIFIED:20241212T214010Z
LOCATION:Trinity Library
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Adventus Spiritual Writing Group
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
